Vitalik Buterin (Ethereum co-founder) has been active with ETH sales today (February 3, 2026), based on on-chain tracking from sources like Lookonchain.
He sold a total of around 493 ETH in the past 8-24 hours, worth approximately $1.16 million (at the time of transactions, with ETH trading around $2,300–$2,400 range).
This aligns with his announced plan from late January 2026: Withdrawing 16,384 ETH (~$38–45 million at the time) from personal wallets to fund multi-year philanthropic and ecosystem goals, including open-source tech, security, privacy, and grants—without drawing from Ethereum Foundation reserves.
